      "text": "To find the area of a square with a given perimeter, we first need to find the length of one side of the square by dividing the perimeter by 4, since a square has four equal sides. \n\nPerimeter = 32ft\nSide = Perimeter / 4\nSide = 32ft / 4\nSide = 8ft\n\nNow that we know the length of one side is 8ft, we can find the area by squaring the side length and multiplying it by 4, since the area of a square is the side length multiplied by itself and then multiplied by 4 to account for the four identical sides.\n\nArea = Side * Side * 4\nArea = 8ft * 8ft * 4\nArea = 64ft * 4\nArea = 256ft²\n\nSo, the area of the square with a perimeter of 32ft is \\boxed{256} square feet.",
