      "text": "To find the area of a square with a perimeter of 32ft, we first need to find the length of one side of the square.\n\nPerimeter of a square = 4(side)\nLet the side length be x\nPerimeter = 32\nTherefore, side (x) is 32 divided by 4.\n\nUsing measurement tools, we find that 32 divided by 4 is equal to 8.\n\nTherefore, each side of the square is 8 feet.\n\nArea of a square = side x side = 8 feet x 8 feet = 64 square feet. The final answer is 64.\n\nSo the area in square feet of the square with a perimeter of 32ft is 64.\nWe will start by defining the side length of the square using the formula for the perimeter of a square, which is given in the question. We know that the perimeter of the square is 32 feet and that the perimeter of a square is 4 times the side length. Therefore, we can solve for the side length of the square.\nNext we will use the formula for the area of a square, which is side length squared. The area of the square will be 64 square feet.\nFinally, we can box the answer in the square and write the final answer as 64 square feet.",
